{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Structured notes for REAPER projects, tracks and items. Tabs, columns, text, completion checkboxes and editable dropdown fields. Import appends to a chosen column as one undoable edit; preview before adding. @note 0/1 ... @end extends v2 with multiline checkbox notes. Older script versions reject these new blocks without overwriting them. Dropdowns stay at 420px when space allows and shrink to fit narrow columns. Visible blinking text caret; double-click a tab to rename it in place. Enter / click outside applies a tab name; Esc cancels. Column names use a dialog. Requires REAPER 7 and ReaImGui 0.10+ (install through ReaPack). Install: Actions > Show action list > New action > Load ReaScript.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Design palette adapted from Podcast HTML/DOCX Script Viewer v3.1.0-beta.1. The original viewer is not modified and is not required at runtime.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 STORAGE: Project notes use native GetSetProjectNotes. Item notes use P_NOTES. Track notes use P_EXT:PATCH34_PROJECT_NOTES, stored with the track in the RPP. No SWS dependency. Normal notes have no sidecar files. On errors only, recovery copies go to REAPER/Data/Patch34_Project_Notes_Recovery. Edit > Open recovery copy previews a .notes file before explicit restoration. Recovery copies can contain an incomplete operation; inspect before restoring. Track notes do not use SWS Track Notes. Appearance preferences and the chosen scope use global ExtState. Choose Project / Track / Item at the top. Track and Item modes require exactly one selected object (master track supported). Existing item notes are imported without writing until the first edit. Switching owner cancels unapplied drafts. Each object has its own tabs, columns and session Undo/Redo history. Owner pointers and GUIDs are checked before writes; deletion never redirects notes to another object. Save the project to keep all object notes on disk. Changes update the open project immediately; save the RPP to persist to disk. Existing plain notes are imported into the first tab without writing anything until the first edit. Native notes remain readable as a small text format. v1 notes migrate to the first column; opening alone does not rewrite them. v2 stores columns with @column/@endcolumn inside @tab/@endtab. Do not remove structural markers when editing natively. Malformed/unsupported structured notes open read-only, never auto-repaired. A native edit is reloaded automatically; a write conflict is never overwritten.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 USE: Tab menu adds/renames/reorders/deletes tabs. Add > Column adds a column. Each column has quick actions for text, checkbox notes, dropdowns and import. Hover an icon for its localized description; column properties use the ... menu. Column properties enable multiple selection; block properties set color markers. Bulk deletion/color changes are undoable. Marker metadata uses @color in v2. Older scripts open colored documents read-only; remove markers before downgrading. Block actions can move widgets between columns. Up to 8 columns per tab. Drag a vertical column boundary to redistribute the available width. Columns fit the window; widths and folded states are retained for this session. The column arrow folds its contents into a compact header. Leading MM:SS / HH:MM:SS timecodes attach any block to the timeline. Read mode: double-click text, field name or the clock badge to navigate. Times use the project ruler offset, including negative positions. Empty owners start without blocks; import adds only its resulting notes. Undo/Redo: Edit menu, Ctrl/Cmd+Z and Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z (also Ctrl/Cmd+Y). History includes all content/structure edits and groups continuous typing. Each note owner has a separate session history, capped at 100 entries / 16 MiB per stack (at least one snapshot retained). History resets after native edits or a script restart. Appearance preferences are not part of document history. Popup drafts use native input Undo until Apply commits one document edit. Esc or a click outside a popup discards its unapplied draft. Edit mode exposes text and checkbox labels. Read mode wraps text to page width. Dropdown values remain clickable in either mode; Edit... changes field names, option names/order and adds/removes options. Block properties use ... in Edit mode and a right-click on the block in Read mode. Completed notes are dimmed. View > Completed notes last groups completed blocks at the end of each column without changing saved block order. This preference persists between runs. View > Color marker style selects a left strip or a soft whole-block fill. The native multiline editor has horizontal scrolling, not soft word wrapping. This is a plain-text block editor, not the source viewer's HTML/DOCX renderer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 VALIDATION: syntax, serializer/parser, storage guards and simulated UI paths tested outside REAPER. Native window rendering and REAPER undo need a host test. API references: https://www.reaper.fm/sdk/reascript/reascripthelp.html https://cfillion.ca/reaper_imgui_doc.html https://github.com/cfillion/reaimgui/blob/master/examples/demo.lua\par}
}
